    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351-a2">

                <pb facs="0466" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg358"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    130.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lespinasse to Mr. Terres.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry for Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port
                                au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-11-22"><hi rendition="#italic">November 22,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vice-Consul-General</hi>:</p>
                <p>In following up my dispatch of the 18th instant I hasten to give you notice that
                    Mr. Frederick Mevs, arrested and incarcerated by the police for the offense of
                    contraband, has been summoned for the first audience of the correctional
                    tribunal of this jurisdiction, audience which will take place on Thursday, the
                    1st of December next, at 10 o’clock in the morning, the very date of the
                    resumption of the ordinary session of the tribunal.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ed. Lespinasse.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
